 "generator": "A0.2 generators, version 2 (dated note of 2026-11-18 in E13.md; version 1 gave the tabular diagnostic of\n`e13_a0_diag.py` a gain below one point for hidden cells; post-hoc revision of the synthetic control, declared). Both keep the real timestamps and calendar. Classes from\nthresholds 0.8/0.4 on a latent factor z = base + 0.4*u + measurement noise (sd 0.03), clipped to [0, 1.6], with\nbase_t(i) = profile_t * amp(i) (two daily dips) and u a persistent field, u_t = 0.97*u_{t-1} + sqrt(1-0.97^2)*shock_t.\n'dependent': amp and the shocks are spatially smoothed by a Gaussian kernel on the UTM coordinates (bandwidth 800 m,\nrow-normalised, shocks rescaled to unit variance): the field is smooth at the scale of the hidden grid cells and\npersistent over hours, so the observed neighbours' history is informative about a hidden node's future beyond the calendar.\n'independent': amp i.i.d. per node and shocks i.i.d. per node and time, no smoothing: any dependence between nodes\nbeyond the shared calendar profile is absent by construction. Nothing of the real target processes enters.",
 "diagnostic": "ADAPTER_SPEC \u00a77, MAE version of `e13.tabular_diagnostic`. PRIVILEGED: both tables are estimated on the validation-hidden\nnodes' own training-origin targets (which the model never sees) and read on validation origins; this measures how much\na tabular predictor gains from the spatial feature, not a bound on the model. Table A: median of z per weekly slot (672)\nof the target time, fallback to the global median when a slot has < `min_count` values. Table B: median within (slot \u00d7\nbin of the spatial feature at the origin), the feature being the input (observed) nodes' z at the origin propagated by the\nREFERENCE operator \u03a3_{k\u2264hops}(A_q)^k and divided by the propagated mass, 32 equal-width bins over [0, 1.6] plus the\nunreachable bin; fallback to Table A's slot median. gain_h = 100\u00b7(MAE_A \u2212 MAE_B)/MAE_A; the diagnostic gain is the mean.\n`slot`/`n_slots` override the weekly slot (development calibration only, `diag-dev`); the protocol uses su.slot (672).",
 "init_stream": 7,
